  "steps": [
    "Cook the Arbi in a pressure cooker for 1 whistle and the skin should coke off easily.",
    "Cut into halves and spray some oil on top and airfry for 15-18 mins on 180 degrees until cripsy and brown on top.",
    "Now smash each piece with a heavy item and coat it in the masala mix.",
    "Spray some oil on top and airfry again for 6-7 mins until crispy on both sides.",
    "Blend everything together and its ready!!",
    "Soak Imli in hot water for 10-15 mins and extract al thr juice from the pulp.",
    "Cook this imli juice with sweetner, sendha namak an red chilli powder for 10 mins until it comes to a boil and thickens a bit.",
    "Cool down and store for 20 days in the fridge!",
    "Assemble the Arbi Tuk Chaat with 150g greek yogurt, chutneys, anaar and handful of dhaniya."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The green chutney and imli chutney are both made from scratch here."
  ],
